<article class="env-example" id="1DA7F5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/1DA7F5">Example <span data-tag="1DA7F5">3.2.5.6</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a small category, and regard $\Nerve (\calC )$ as an object of $(\sSet )_{/ \Nerve (\calC )}$ via the identity map. Then ${\mathfrak F}_{\Nerve (\calC )}(\calC ) \in (\sSet )^{\calC }$ can be identified with the functor $C \mapsto \Nerve (\calC _{/C})$. </p>
